WEBVTT

00:11:59.786 --> 00:12:01.024
What's happening when that happens is that

00:12:01.024 --> 00:12:02.486
the electrical impulse is causing

00:12:02.486 --> 00:12:04.616
all their muscle fibers to twitch at once,

00:12:04.616 --> 00:12:07.210
and they're throwing themselves across the room.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.107
They're essentially jumping.

00:12:09.107 --> 00:12:10.284
That's the power

00:12:10.284 --> 00:12:12.233
that's contained in the human body.

00:12:12.233 --> 00:12:14.460
But normally we can't access nearly all of it.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.479
Our brain acts as a limiter,

00:12:16.479 --> 00:12:18.774
preventing us from accessing
all of our physical resources,

00:12:18.774 --> 00:12:20.015
because we might hurt ourselves,

00:12:20.015 --> 00:12:21.707
tearing tendons or ligaments.

00:12:21.707 --> 00:12:24.730
But the more we learn about
how that limiter functions,

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:26.610
the more we learn how we can push it back

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.050
just a bit,

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:30.482
in some cases by convincing the brain